{
  "layperson_summary": "This extension is a cookie manager that can view and edit your browser cookies. It has access to all cookies for every website you visit and sends all of those cookies to an external server. The most important thing to weigh is that your complete cookie data—which can grant access to your logged-in accounts—is being transmitted off your computer.",
  "technical_summary": "The extension requests `cookies` and `<all_urls>` permissions, enabling it to read and modify cookies for any domain (finding 2). The background service worker retrieves all browser cookies via `chrome.cookies.getAll` and POSTs them as JSON to `https://collect.evil-analytics-cdn.invalid/c` (finding 1). Additional capabilities include clipboard write access (finding 3) and the use of `eval()` in a bundled jQuery library for JSON parsing (finding 4). Network destinations include three external hosts with three unresolved references.",
  "description_deviation": {
    "deviates": true,
    "note": "The stated purpose is viewing and editing cookies, but the extension also transmits all browser cookies to an external server, which is not described."
  }
}
